flowchart LR
  %% QUESTION THIS DIAGRAM ANSWERS: diagrams 07a and 07b show the path when every check succeeds. What happens when one check fails, and where can a reader of the records see that it failed?
  %% READING: each row is one kind of failure, in the order of the process. The rows are separate cases, not a sequence. Column 1 = what fails. Column 2 = who acts and how. Column 3 = where the transaction continues. Column 4 (grey) = the record or report in which the failure is visible.
  %% WHY IT MATTERS FOR A PROCESS MODEL: each row is a path that leaves the main sequence. A model that contains only the main sequence cannot represent unpaid obligations, lapsed authority or recovered payments.
  %% SOURCES: row 1, changes of allotment and their approval [NBC599 s.3.13]; BTMS refuses an obligation above the allotment and a payment above the cash allocation [CL2025-8]. Row 2, take-over of a terminated contract by negotiated procurement [IRR12009 s.35.3]. Row 4, a regular NCA lapses at the end of the quarter, additional NCAs, and the regular NCA covers payables of the current and of earlier years [NBC599 s.4.2]; aging of unpaid obligations in FAR 3 and monthly disbursements in FAR 4 [JC2019-1]. Row 5, the bank notes a non-payment in the remarks column when the name or account number of the creditor does not agree with its records, and the list of bank-validated ADAs is proof of payment [CL2018-14]. Row 6, unused balances revert to the unappropriated surplus of the General Fund [NBC599 s.3.6]. Row 7, transfers are not disbursements until the receiver has used them for accepted deliveries [NBC599 s.3.4]; report FAR 1-C [JC2019-1]. Row 8, notices of suspension and of disallowance, appeal, finality, order of execution [COA2009-006].
  %% WEAKNESS REPORTED: the stock of expenditure arrears in 2023 was above 10 percent of expenditure (indicator 22.1, score D) [PEFA2025].
  %% GENERAL KNOWLEDGE, NOT OPENED IN A SOURCE HERE: row 3 as a whole; in row 2 the form by which an obligation is reduced or cancelled; in row 5 what the agency does after the bank reports a non-payment; in row 7 the return of unused cash. These steps are in the Government Accounting Manual, which I could not open.

  S(["A step of the<br/>main path fails<br/>(main path: 07a)"])

  S --> A1["1  NO ALLOTMENT BALANCE<br/>for the obligation request"] --> A2["The budget unit refuses the request.<br/>In BTMS the system blocks it"] --> A3["The agency asks for a change of allotment<br/>or for a new release (see 05e)"] --> A4["Registry of allotments<br/>and obligations"]:::rec

  S --> B1["2  DELIVERY NOT ACCEPTED<br/>goods or works fail the inspection"] --> B2["No acceptance report is issued.<br/>The supplier must correct the delivery"] --> B3["If the contract is ended, another supplier<br/>may complete the work, chosen by negotiated procurement"] --> B4["The obligation stays open,<br/>or is reduced"]:::rec

  S --> C1["3  CLAIM INCOMPLETE<br/>a document is missing or wrong"] --> C2["The accounting unit<br/>returns the claim"] --> C3["The claimant completes it<br/>and submits it again"] --> C4["No journal entry before the<br/>voucher is certified"]:::rec

  S --> D1["4  NO CASH AUTHORITY<br/>the NCA is fully used, or the NCA<br/>of the quarter has lapsed"] --> D2["The agency requests an<br/>additional NCA from DBM"] --> D3["Unpaid at the end of the year: a due and<br/>demandable obligation, paid from<br/>an NCA of the next year"] --> D4["FAR 3 (age of unpaid obligations)<br/>FAR 4 (monthly disbursements)"]:::rec

  S --> E1["5  BANK CANNOT CREDIT THE PAYEE<br/>name or account number does<br/>not agree with the bank records"] --> E2["The bank writes the non-payment in the<br/>remarks column of the payment order"] --> E3["The agency corrects the data of the<br/>payee and orders the payment again"] --> E4["List of bank-validated payment<br/>advices. Bank reconciliation"]:::rec

  S --> F1["6  AUTHORITY NOT USED<br/>the validity of the appropriation ends<br/>and a balance is not obligated"] --> F2["The authority to obligate<br/>the balance ends"] --> F3["The balance reverts to the unappropriated<br/>surplus of the General Fund"] --> F4["FAR 1, unobligated<br/>balances"]:::rec

  S --> G1["7  TRANSFERRED MONEY NOT USED<br/>by the agency or local government<br/>that received it"] --> G2["The source agency may not<br/>report it as disbursed"] --> G3["The receiver reports the use<br/>or returns the unused cash"] --> G4["FAR 1-C (transfers between<br/>agencies and their liquidation)"]:::rec

  S --> H1["8  IRREGULAR PAYMENT FOUND AFTER PAYMENT<br/>by the COA auditor"] --> H2["Notice of suspension (documents required)<br/>or notice of disallowance (payment rejected)"] --> H3["Appeal. When the decision is final:<br/>order of execution against the<br/>persons liable (see 09b)"] --> H4["Audit notices and the<br/>statements of the auditor"]:::rec


